        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0883" n="1841" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1841"/>

                <head>No. 18.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White
                        to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 767.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instructions
                    numbered 864, of May 1, and to previous correspondence, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith, for your information, a copy of Sir James Fergusson’s reply to
                    a question asked by Mr. Gourley in the House of Commons on the 4th instant, from
                    which you will observe that the Canadian Government have cautioned persons
                    engaged in sealing expeditions in Behring Sea against using force in the event
                    of their being interfered with by our officers.</p>
                <p>I have etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d541-a1.xml" xpointer="d541-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
